s 0.4 per day in storage, but a full 9 if it spoils.\n  - With demand swinging about 30% day to day, ordering above the forecast pays off. So the larger plans (7, then 4, then 0) should beat the smaller plan 5.\n- **Total ordered vs. expected demand:**\n  - Product 0: candidate 0 orders 852 units against an expected demand of about 827 for days 5–29.\n  - Product 1: candidate 0 orders 1,122 units against about 1,082.\n  - Candidate 7 orders roughly 10–15% more than candidate 0. Candidate 4 orders more product 0 and slightly less product 1.\n- **Candidate 1:** it is candidate 0 with the day-14 and day-20 orders split across two days. That adds 110 in fees and reduces overflow near the day-25 spike of product 1 (demand 102). I put it about level with candidate 0.\n- **Candidate 2:** it uses the same two-day rhythm shifted by one day, ordering about 886 of product 0 and 1,122 of product 1. That's comparable to candidate 0, with a little more product 0.\n\n**My top four:** 7, 4, 2 and 0, with 1 close behind. The likely bottom four are 5, 6 and 3, with 1 also near the cut line."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4926, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4926}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T07:36:07.118Z", "request_id": "req_011CgW9G6QEpPAWLuTpq13E3"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LZk5UhPwbqBwYPBZtbtqHn", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_