nd 4** sit in that zone. Candidate 2 also times its deliveries well: the large order arrives on day 20, the product 0 spike (83), and the last order lands on day 28.\n- **Candidate 1** is the same as Candidate 0 but has two extra ordering days (+110 in fees), offset by better timing around the day-20 spike. It's a toss-up.\n- **Candidate 7** over-orders a lot: about +130 of product 0 and about +170 of product 1. Much of that becomes unsold stock at the end (roughly 2000 in purchases). The cash caps early on partly offset this, so it's uncertain.\n- **Candidate 5** is below average demand on both products and gets cut further by the early cash shortage, so it runs short.\n- **Candidate 3** orders every 3 days and saves about 220 in fees. But each delivery is around 230 units, so with any leftover stock it overflows the 232-unit warehouse. Product 1 is accepted second, so its excess is what gets lost. It also has more holding cost and too little product 0.\n- **Candidate 6** orders daily: 25 ordering days against 13, about +660 in fees, for no real benefit."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5040, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5040}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T07:36:42.181Z", "request_id": "req_011CgW9GYCnDKehaoXtiGXhv"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01M7g2hwYunaxJfEwBLPoDgg", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null